\section{URL enumeration}{

SIAIA is a server-rendered ASP.NET MVC application. The listing lives at
\verb{https://siaia.apambiente.pt/ProcessoAIA?pagina=<n>} (1-based pages, ~100
rows/page). Each listing row links to a detail page
\verb{/ProcessoAIA/Detalhes/\{pro_id\}} and a document list
\verb{/ListaDocumentos?pro_id=\{pro_id\}}. The handler walks pages with a page
generator (see \code{stream_crawl()}); an out-of-range page returns an empty
table body, which terminates the crawl. The canonical record URL is the
detail page \verb{https://siaia.apambiente.pt/ProcessoAIA/Detalhes/\{pro_id\}}.

Per record, metadata is read from the detail page's \emph{Campo / Conteúdo}
table (sidecar-first via the cache), and attachments from the document
list.
}

\section{Attachments}{
 per-phase section split:
SIAIA renders each document with a Portuguese \emph{type} label (e.g.
\emph{"DIA - Declaração Impacte Ambiental"}, \emph{"EIA Relatório Sintese (RS)"},
\emph{"Parecer comissão de avaliação"}, \emph{"Relatório da consulta pública"}).
The portal does not print explicit phase headings, so the handler derives
a coarse \strong{phase} from each label and groups by it. Phases:
\itemize{
\item \code{dia} — \emph{DIA} (Declaração de Impacte Ambiental — the decision).
\item \code{eia} — \emph{EIA} documents (relatório síntese, RNT, anexos, peças
desenhadas, projeto, elementos adicionais — the substantive dossier).
\item \code{consulta_publica} — \emph{Consulta Pública} documents.
\item \code{parecer} — \emph{Parecer} documents (e.g. Parecer da Comissão de Avaliação).
\item \code{outros} — anything that matches none of the above.
}

Each phase that carries documents becomes its own parallel list-column
\verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} / \verb{local_path_<slug>} (the slug is \code{ascii_slug()}
of the phase). \code{attachment_urls} / \code{local_path} are the deduplicated union
across all phases (required by the planscanR schema). PDF URLs are direct
and of the form \verb{https://siaia.apambiente.pt/AIADOC/AIA\{n\}/\{file\}.pdf}
(some documents are \code{.zip} archives — these are kept as attachments too).
}

\section{Filter coverage (v0.1)}{

SIAIA offers server-side authority/year filters, but for v1 every filter is
applied \strong{client-side} for simplicity and predictability:
\itemize{
\item \code{query} — case-insensitive substring match on \code{title} (the project
designation).
\item \code{date_range} — matched against \code{date_decision} when the detail page
exposes a full \emph{Data da decisão}; for records that only carry a decision
\emph{year} (the listing's \emph{Ano Decisão}), the year is matched against the
range instead.
\item \code{limit} — caps the total number of records returned.
}
}

\section{Performance}{

The register holds a few thousand AIA procedures across a few dozen listing
pages. A cold crawl is one listing GET per page plus one detail GET per
record (sidecar-first, so repeat runs are fast). To be polite to the shared
government portal, PT requests are throttled to 5 requests per second by
default; override via \code{getOption("planscanR.pt_throttle_rate")}
(requests/sec; falsy disables).
}

